<title>INDIA: India 96/97 coffee exports fall to 164,403 tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 coffee exports fall to 164,403 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>India exported 164,403 tonnes of coffee worth $410.75 million in 1996/97 (April-March) compared with 170,990 tonnes in 1995/96 valued at $456.00 million, Commerce Minister B.B. Ramaiah said on Friday.</p>
<p>Ramaiah told the lower house of parliament India had set a coffee export target of 150,000 tonnes for 1997/98.</p>
<p>It was aiming at the United States, Japan, Russia and the Middle East countries for boosting its coffee exports.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
